Answer the APFS queries FileProvider makes for regular files with "none" on HFS+, as 1142 did for folders: with 1142
the On My iPhone root resolved and DocumentManager found Downloads, but Safari's .download placeholder still failed
to arrive there. A failed-syscall trace (sweetsyserr=LocalStorageFileProvider,fileproviderd) showed an ffsctl
ENOTTY in LocalStorageFileProvider, which logged "can't obtain VFSItem for .../File Provider Storage/Downloads/
X.download [25: Inappropriate ioctl for device]"; fileproviderd: "move-writer: resolving item at URL ... failed"
(Cocoa 256), DocumentManager's FPMoveOperation reverted and Safari waited at 100%. FileProviderDaemon+0x1c373c reads
the item's purgeable info, ffsctl(fd, _IOR('J', 109, 48 bytes)) (0x40304a6d), and fails the item on any error;
fpfs_get_purgeable_info() reads the same (flags at 0, a value at 0x20). The pristine info, _IOR('J', 123, 16 bytes)
(0x40104a7b), is read by fpfs_t_fget_is_pristine()/fpfs_t_fget_pristine_time() and fpfs_get_purgeable_flags().
Nothing on HFS is purgeable or pristine: both are answered with zeros.

diff --git a/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c b/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c
--- a/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c
+++ b/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c
@@ -3168,6 +3168,24 @@
 	case SWEET_APFSIOC_GET_SYNC_ROOT_FLAG:
 		*(uint32_t *)ap->a_data = 0;
 		return 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * The same lookup for a regular file: FileProviderDaemon (+0x1c373c) reads the per-item purgeable info (48
+	 * bytes: flags at 0, a time in ns at 0x10, counts at 0x18 and 0x20, also fpfs_get_purgeable_info()) and fails
+	 * the item on an error, so every file in On My iPhone was "can't obtain VFSItem ... [25: Inappropriate ioctl
+	 * for device]" and Safari's .download placeholder could not be moved into Downloads (FPMoveOperation, Cocoa 256).
+	 * The pristine info (16 bytes, fpfs_t_fget_is_pristine(), fpfs_get_purgeable_flags()) is asked for the same
+	 * files. Nothing on HFS is purgeable or pristine: all zero.
+	 */
+#define SWEET_APFSIOC_GET_PURGEABLE_INFO   _IOR('J', 109, uint64_t[6])
+#define SWEET_APFSIOC_GET_PRISTINE_INFO    _IOR('J', 123, uint64_t[2])
+	case SWEET_APFSIOC_GET_PURGEABLE_INFO:
+		bzero(ap->a_data, 6 * sizeof(uint64_t));
+		return 0;
+
+	case SWEET_APFSIOC_GET_PRISTINE_INFO:
+		bzero(ap->a_data, 2 * sizeof(uint64_t));
+		return 0;
 #endif
 
 	default:
